+## A `beforeSession` that throws
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws still rejects the caller, and its throw reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn, so `onError` fires with the thrown error and `afterSession` fires after it with no flag to tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished" — the recorded answer, which makes idempotence the deployer's job: a hook that releases in `afterSession` what `beforeSession` allocated must guard the release. What such a hook may assume about how much of the turn happened is that only `beforeSession` ran — no user-input hook, no provider call, no tool, no `afterModelResponse` ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
